01. EC2 Lifecycle

Understand this:

Pending
   ↓
Running
   ↓
Stopping
   ↓
Stopped
   ↓
Starting
   ↓
Running

Running
   ↓
Terminating
   ↓
Terminated

Important:

Stop
Instance is powered off.
EBS volumes normally remain.

Terminate
Instance is permanently removed.
Root EBS may also be deleted depending on its DeleteOnTermination setting.



02. Stop vs Terminate
Interview question:

What is the difference between stopping and terminating an EC2 instance?

Answer:

Stop
→ VM shuts down
→ Can start again
→ EBS generally remains

Terminate
→ Instance is deleted
→ Cannot restart that same instance
→ EBS deletion depends on configuration


EC2 Hibernate:
EC2 Instance
 
• Introducing EC2 Hibernate: 
• The in-memory (RAM) state is preserved
• The instance boot is much faster! 
(the OS is not stopped / restarted)
• Under the hood: the RAM state is written 
to a file in the root EBS volume
• The root EBS volume must be encrypted
• Use cases: 
• Long-running processing
• Saving the RAM state
• Services that take time to initialize

