04. EC2 Image Builder 
It is an AWS service used to automatically create, customize, test, and distribute machine images, such as AMIs.

Instead of manually creating an EC2 server every time, you create a standardized golden AMI automatically.

Simple idea

Without Image Builder:

Launch EC2
   ↓
Install Java
   ↓
Install Docker
   ↓
Install CloudWatch Agent
   ↓
Install Security tools
   ↓
Configure settings
   ↓
Create AMI manually

With Image Builder:

Image Builder Pipeline
        ↓
Launch temporary EC2
        ↓
Install/configure software
        ↓
Run tests
        ↓
Create AMI
        ↓
Distribute AMI
        ↓
Use AMI in EC2 / ASG
1. What problem does Image Builder solve?

Imagine your company has 50 EC2 instances.

Every instance needs:

Amazon Linux
Docker
AWS CLI
CloudWatch Agent
Security Agent
Java
Company certificates
Monitoring configuration

If engineers manually configure every server:

EC2-1 → configure manually
EC2-2 → configure manually
EC2-3 → configure manually
...
EC2-50 → configure manually

You can easily end up with:

EC2-1 → Docker 28
EC2-2 → Docker 27
EC2-3 → Docker 28
EC2-4 → missing CloudWatch agent

This creates configuration drift.

Image Builder solves this by creating a standardized image.

              EC2 Image Builder
                     ↓
             Golden AMI
                     ↓
       ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
       ↓             ↓             ↓
     EC2-1         EC2-2         EC2-3

All instances start from the same baseline.


05. Monitoring
EC2 integrates with:
CloudWatch

You can monitor things like:

CPUUtilization
NetworkIn
NetworkOut
Disk-related metrics
Status checks

Important distinction:

EC2 basic monitoring doesn't automatically give you every OS-level metric such as memory utilization.

For memory/disk-space/process-level metrics, you typically install/configure the CloudWatch agent or another monitoring agent.




06. EC2 Status Checks
Two important concepts:

System Status Check
Instance Status Check

System check:
Problem with underlying AWS infrastructure.

Instance check:
Problem associated with the instance/OS.

Example:

EC2 unreachable
      ↓
Check status checks
      ↓
Determine infrastructure vs instance issue
